Spec: Manager

Purpose:
  Own the operator's controller runtime: build the @Manager — the @Arc-shared @Diagnostics and
    @Metrics pair ./main.rs hands to actix — build the one shared @Context every reconcile
    receives (rendered engine, env-baked `base_context`, JukeBox package cache), probe that all
    four CRDs answer, and hand back the four boxed controller futures ./main.rs races. Also
    own the JukeBox package cache itself: @JukeCacheItem, its diff/upsert rules, and the async
    accessors the reconciles call. Futures are lazy here — nothing is polled until ./main.rs
    selects on them — and the reconcile bodies, finalizers, scan-job rules and @Action backoffs
    those futures run belong to the kind specs referenced below, not to this file.

References:
  ./lib.sdd — @Context defined here is the trait's ctx carrier, and this @Manager is what the
    crate root republishes as its `pub use` name; the @get_client_name identity split crosses
    this file only through @common::@context::@get_client_async used by the context seed
    (see below).
  ./metrics.sdd — @Metrics, its four prefixed registries and label rules; @Manager::metrics
    only encodes what that spec builds.
  ./main.sdd — sole caller of @Manager::new, @Manager::metrics and @Manager::diagnostics; the
    @tokio::@select! race, the three route answers, exit codes and every panic that crosses
    into exit `101` are frozen there.
  ./jukebox.sdd, ./instance_common.sdd, ./instanceservice.sdd, ./instancesystem.sdd,
    ./instancetenant.sdd — specs pending; they own the @reconcile and @error_policy functions
    wired here, the force-scan/finalizer/job-template rules, the @last_event writers
    (@ctx.diagnostics.write()), the cache call sites, and the `base_context` consumers.
  /common/src/jukebox.sdd — @JukeBox, @JukeBoxSpec::pull_secret, @JukeBoxStatus::packages and
    @JukeBox::list (per-call @get_client_async client build, cluster-scope list).
  /common/src/context.sdd — @common::context::@get_client_async and its @panic! text
    `cannot create the Kubernetes client: {e}` (reached via the seed, see Handles).
  /common/src/vynilpackage.sdd — @VynilPackage, the cached payload and the @Eq definition the
    diff runs on.
  /common/src/handlebarshandler.sdd — @HandleBars::@new and @register_partial_dir, including
    the core @is_dir gate that answers a missing directory with a silent @Ok no-op.
  /common/src/instanceservice.sdd, /common/src/instancesystem.sdd,
    /common/src/instancetenant.sdd — the three namespaced CR models watched.

Depends on:
  @kube (locked `3.1.0`) — @Client::@try_default, @Api::@all, @ListParams, @ObjectList,
    @ResourceExt::@name_any, @runtime::controller::@Controller, @watcher::@Config,
    @events::@Reporter; on that build @events::@Reporter implements @From<&str> reading the OS
    hostname into the `instance` field.
  @common — @common::handlebarshandler::@HandleBars, @common::vynilpackage::@VynilPackage,
    @common::@DEFAULT_AGENT_IMAGE and @JukeBox::@list.
  @futures — @FutureExt::@boxed, @StreamExt, @future::@BoxFuture, @future::@ready.
  @tokio::sync::@RwLock — every shared-state guard in this file (async, not std).
  @chrono — @DateTime<@Utc>, @Utc::@now; @serde and @serde_json — @Serialize on @Diagnostics,
    the @json! carrier of `base_context`.
  @prometheus_client `0.24.x` text format — @encode_registry and @encode_eof inside
    @Manager::metrics.
  @std::env — the six startup-variable reads pinned in Must.
  @std::collections::@BTreeMap, @std::sync::@Arc, @std::path::@PathBuf.

Must:
  Define @Manager as `#[derive(Clone, @Default, @Debug)] pub struct Manager` with exactly two
    private fields: @diagnostics @Arc<@RwLock<@Diagnostics>> and @metrics @Arc<@Metrics>;
    @Default constructs a fresh @Diagnostics and a fresh @Metrics, @Clone shares both Arcs.
  Boot exactly once through @Manager::@new in this order: @Client::@try_default (@Err →
    @panic! `cannot create the Kubernetes client: {e}`) → @Self::@default → @build_context
    awaited → four cluster-scope @Api::@all handles (@JukeBox, @TenantInstance,
    @ServiceInstance, @SystemInstance) → four probes, each @list of @ListParams::@default
    with @limit(`1`), in order JukeBox, TenantInstance, SystemInstance, ServiceInstance, each
    @Err → @panic! `is a CRD installed? {e}` → build the four controllers → return the tuple of
    the @Manager plus the four @BoxFuture values in the destructure order stated in Exposes.
    @Manager::new has no @Result channel: success builds everything, failure kills the
    process.
  Build each future by one identical shape — @Controller::@new(@Api,
    @Config::@default().@any_semantic()).@run(kind::@reconcile, kind::@error_policy,
    @Arc<@Context> clone) then @filter_map keeping @Ok(@Action) only then @for_each dropping
    that @Action then @boxed — giving @BoxFuture<'static, ()> per kind, with the pairs
    @jukebox::@reconcile and @jukebox::@error_policy, @instancetenant::@reconcile and
    @instancetenant::@error_policy, @instancesystem::@reconcile and
    @instancesystem::@error_policy, @instanceservice::@reconcile and
    @instanceservice::@error_policy. All four share the one @Arc<@Context>; the futures are
    lazy until ./main.rs polls them.
  Watch exactly the default @watcher::@Config plus @ListSemantic::@Any (@any_semantic), so
    metadata-only events reach reconcile too, with no label or field selectors and no namespace
    narrowing (the @Api::@all handles stream all four kinds cluster-wide); no selectors, drain
    conditions or grace settings are configured here.
  Drop the controller stream's @Err half at the @filter_map: every failed-reconcile event is
    discarded uninspected and unlogged by this file, so failure backoff and visibility live
    entirely in the kind modules' @error_policy and in kube-runtime's own machinery; the
    dropped @Action never feeds back — requeue decisions were already applied internally by
    @Controller::@run.
  Share state through the Arcs only: @build_context stores @Clone copies of the @Manager
    @metrics and @diagnostics Arcs into @Context, so a reconcile writing through
    @ctx.diagnostics or @ctx.metrics mutates what this @Manager — and every actix @Data clone
    of it — later reads.
  Read startup configuration from exactly six environment variables, once per process, each
    through @std::env::@var plus @unwrap_or_else — a present-but-empty value passes through as
    `""`, a non-Unicode or absent one falls to the default:
    `CONTROLLER_BASE_DIR`: default `./operator`; sole use is the partial-dir path
      `{CONTROLLER_BASE_DIR}/templates` (working-directory-relative by default).
    `VYNIL_NAMESPACE`: default `vynil-system`.
    `AGENT_IMAGE`: default @common::@DEFAULT_AGENT_IMAGE — `docker.io/sebt3/vynil-agent:0.7.7`.
    `AGENT_ACCOUNT`: default `vynil-agent`.
    `AGENT_LOG_LEVEL`: default `info`.
    `TENANT_LABEL`: default `vynil.solidite.fr/tenant`.
    Env read order: `CONTROLLER_BASE_DIR` before the renderer, the other five during
    @Context construction after the seed list.
  Build @Context's `base_context` as a @json! object with exactly the keys `vynil_namespace`,
    `agent_image`, `service_account`, `log_level` and `label_key` carrying those six reads — the
    JSON key differs from the env name in three cases (`AGENT_ACCOUNT` → `service_account`,
    `AGENT_LOG_LEVEL` → `log_level`, `TENANT_LABEL` → `label_key`) — and keep it immutable for
    the process lifetime; reconciles clone it per render and add per-object keys (owned by the
    kind specs). This key-set is this file's bake; `TENANT_LABEL` is additionally re-read
    per call inside @common::@context::@get_labels, a separate lane this file does not control.
  Register `register_partial_dir(@PathBuf)` failures as warn-only inside @build_context —
    @tracing::@warn! `Registering template generated: {e}` — and boot on regardless; the core
    @is_dir gate makes a missing `templates` directory a silent @Ok no-op, so neither the warn
    nor a failure marks the common broken-renderer case.
  Seed the package cache inside @build_context from @JukeBox::@list(): @Ok builds a fresh
    @BTreeMap keyed by @name_any over the items whose @status is @Some — entries carry
    @spec.pull_secret and @status.packages cloned — logs @tracing::@debug!
    `Initialize packages cache` and `Initialize packages cache done`, and replaces the cache
    even when the seed map is empty; @Err logs @tracing::@warn! `While listing jukebox:
    {:?}` (Debug formatting of the error) and boot continues with an empty cache. JukeBoxes
    without a status never enter the cache here.
  Define @Context as `#[derive(Clone)] pub struct Context` with exactly six `pub` fields in
    order: @client @kube::@Client, @diagnostics @Arc<@RwLock<@Diagnostics>>, @metrics
    @Arc<@Metrics>, @renderer @HandleBars<'static>, @base_context @serde_json::@Value, @packages
    @Arc<@RwLock<@BTreeMap<@String, @JukeCacheItem>>>; the hand-written @Debug substitutes the
    literal `kube::Client` for @client and `handlebars::HandleBars` for @renderer and
    live-formats @diagnostics, @base_context and the whole @packages map — every cached package
    body — while @metrics delegates to @Metrics. The shared @renderer is consumed by clone at
    each reconcile (kind specs), never mutated in place through @Context.
  Define @JukeCacheItem as `#[derive(Debug)] pub struct` with `pub` fields @pull_secret
    @Option<@String> and @packages @Vec<@VynilPackage>, no other derives.
  Gate every cache mutation on @name_any as key — kube-core `3.1.0` resolution `metadata.name`
    → `metadata.generate_name` → `""`, so several nameless JukeBoxes share the single `""`
    entry; @BTreeMap keeps entries name-ordered.
  Compute staleness through @cache_entry_differs(@BTreeMap, @JukeBox) (@crate-visible): a
    @None @status answers @false always, otherwise @is_none_or — an absent key answers @true,
    and a present entry answers @true only when its @packages vector `!=` @status.packages or
    its @pull_secret `!=` @spec.pull_secret; unchanged status answers @false.
  Apply @upsert_cache_entry(&mut @BTreeMap, @JukeBox) (@crate-visible): @None @status is a
    silent no-op that leaves any existing entry untouched — neither refresh nor removal — and
    otherwise @insert overwrites the key with @spec.pull_secret and @status.packages cloned.
  Expose the cache to reconciles through four @async methods on @Context, each holding the
    tokio lock only across its own call: @Context::upsert_jukebox_cache (write lock plus
    @upsert_cache_entry), @Context::remove_jukebox_cache(@name) (write lock @remove, the
    returned @Option discarded, so an absent key is a silent success returning nothing),
    @Context::cache_needs_update (read lock plus @cache_entry_differs), and
    @Context::set_package_cache(@ObjectList<@JukeBox>).
  Rebuild in @Context::set_package_cache from the given list only — no cluster call: fresh
    map from the @Some-status items, a log-line `jukes` string of every item name joined by `,`
    (@reduce, `""` for an empty list), and a package count summed with @saturating_add;
    an empty rebuild logs @tracing::@warn! `No packages found from the jukebox list
    ({jukes}) to update the cache` and keeps the previous cache byte-for-byte, while a
    non-empty rebuild logs @tracing::@info! `Updating packages cache with {count} packages
    from {len} jukebox: {jukes}`, wholesale-replaces the cache, and closes with
    @tracing::@debug! `Updating packages cache done`. This empty-guard differs from the
    @build_context unconditional replace, and the method has no caller in the workspace (Tasks).
  Define @Diagnostics as `#[derive(Clone, @Debug, @Serialize)] pub struct` with `pub`
    @last_event @DateTime<@Utc> and `#[serde(skip)]` @reporter @kube::runtime::events::@Reporter;
    @Default stamps @last_event with @Utc::@now at construction — boot time until a reconcile
    first overwrites it — and @reporter from the literal `vynil-controller` via the
    kube-runtime `3.1.0` @From<&str> conversion, which writes that literal into the
    `controller` field and fills `instance` from the OS hostname. @reporter never serializes
    anywhere and no code reads or rewrites it after @default; this file only stores it while
    reconciles (./jukebox.rs, ./instance_common.rs) own every @last_event write.
  Render @Manager::metrics as `#[must_use] pub fn @metrics(&self) -> @String`: encode exactly
    @reg_box, @reg_sys, @reg_svc, @reg_tnt in that order through @encode_registry, logging
    @tracing::@error! `encoding prometheus registry failed: {e}` and continuing to the next
    registry on @Err — bytes already appended by a failing registry stay in the buffer — then
    one @encode_eof whose @Err logs `encoding prometheus EOF failed: {e}`; return the buffer
    unconditionally, whatever failed (the `200` route decision is ./main.rs).
  Export @Manager::diagnostics as @async @pub fn returning the @clone of the snapshot taken
    under the read guard of @Diagnostics.

Exposes:
  @Manager — `pub` struct shared with the actix layer via ./main.rs; surface is @Manager::@new,
    @Manager::metrics, @Manager::diagnostics and the derive trio @Clone, @Default and @Debug;
    re-exported at the crate root by ./lib.rs.
  @Manager::new — @async @pub fn returning (@Manager, four @BoxFuture<'static, ()>) in JukeBox,
    Tenant, System, Service order; panics are its only failure channel.
  @Context — `pub` struct, @Clone plus hand-written @Debug; the sole @Context type of the
    ./lib.sdd @Reconciler contract and of all four controller wires.
  @Context::upsert_jukebox_cache, @Context::remove_jukebox_cache, @Context::cache_needs_update,
    @Context::set_package_cache — the four `pub async` cache accessors.
  @cache_entry_differs, @upsert_cache_entry — `pub(crate)` fn free functions; used here plus
    ./jukebox.rs tests build their maps.
  @Diagnostics — `pub` struct with @last_event and @reporter fields and the @Default impl.
  @JukeCacheItem — `pub` struct, cache map value.

Accepts:
  The six environment variables of Must, read once at @build_context, with every oddity
    (unset, empty, non-Unicode) taking a defined arm; nothing else is read from the process.
  A cluster reachable for discovery: @Manager::new takes no argument and preconditions on
    kubeconfig/in-cluster config through @Client::@try_default, and needs the four CRDs
    installed (the `limit=1` probes), having already survived — or silently swallowed — the
    seed list.
  Borrowed @JukeBox references for @cache_entry_differs and @upsert_cache_entry, validated no
    further than the @Option state of @status: @name_any on a nameless object is accepted as
    `""`, and @spec.pull_secret is an unvalidated secret name.
  A borrowed @ObjectList<@JukeBox> to @set_package_cache; the list is cloned, never the cluster
    asked. @Context::remove_jukebox_cache accepts any @name text.
  Preconditions the callers own: @Diagnostics and caches are only touched from a tokio runtime
    (all locks are tokio @RwLock); each @BoxFuture is polled by ./main.rs only.

Returns:
  @Manager::new — the @Manager plus four boxed futures, returned only after all four probes
    answer; the @Manager clone feeds `@Data` in ./main.rs.
  @cache_entry_differs and @Context::cache_needs_update — @bool staleness; @upsert_cache_entry,
    @Context::upsert_jukebox_cache, @Context::remove_jukebox_cache, @Context::set_package_cache
    and @Diagnostics construction return `()`.
  @Manager::metrics — the concatenated OpenMetrics text in the four-registry order above,
    possibly missing a registry or `# EOF` on encoder failure.
  @Manager::diagnostics — a cloned @Diagnostics snapshot taken under the read guard;
    @JukeCacheItem fields are the status payload cloned at insert time.

Raises:
  No typed errors. Nothing here returns @Result or an @Error — @Manager::new's contract is
    future-or-process-death, and @set_package_cache and @build_context launder every fallible
    leg into logs.
  @panic! `cannot create the Kubernetes client: {e}` from @Manager::new's own
    @Client::@try_default, and @panic! `is a CRD installed? {e}` from each of the four probes —
    the four share that one text, so the failed kind is identifiable only from {e}.
  In-transit panic: the @JukeBox::@list seed builds its own client through
    @common::@context::@get_client_async, which @panic! with the same
    `cannot create the Kubernetes client: {e}` text from that site for a cluster the first
    client saw fine; an API-level list failure instead returns @Err and is warn-logged.
  No @unwrap or @expect exists in the file; the @reduce, @unwrap_or_else and @is_none_or legs
    are non-panicking. The panics above are the file's (and the process's) only abrupt ends
    from here.

Handles:
  Probe order vs seed order — a missing Tenant/System/Service CRD still panics through the
    probes even though @build_context (and its JukeBox seed) already completed; a missing
    JukeBox CRD first yields the seed warn, then the first probe panics.
  A box whose status vanished — @cache_needs_update answers @false and @upsert_cache_entry
    no-ops, so the stale pre-removal entry survives in the full cache until @cleanup's removal
    (./jukebox.rs); nothing here ever prunes by age — this cache has no TTL.
  Nameless JukeBoxes — keyed `""`; a fresh-`generate_name`-only box caches under that text
    until the name lands, then re-keys on the next upsert, orphaning the old key until a
    @remove on the new name only never reclaims it.
  Empty package cache at startup — the seed replaces unconditionally (empty means empty),
    while @set_package_cache refuses to empty a populated cache (see Tasks `[?]` for the dead
    lane).
  Partial metrics bodies — a failing registry is skipped after logging, later registries still
    encode, a failing EOF just logs; the returned string is whatever accumulated.
  Lock contention — every accessor takes a tokio @RwLock await, no guard is held across an
    await on other state, so a slow writer (big @insert) only delays readers.
  @Debug of @Context on an arbitrarily large cache prints every cached package — a diagnostics
    cost, not an error.
  `TENANT_LABEL` double-read — the one bake here feeds templates;
    @common::@context::@get_labels re-reads the env per call, so the two can diverge within one
    process after a deployment edit without restart.

Tasks:
  [x] Cache pure-function coverage exists and is green: @cache_entry_differs_when_not_in_cache,
      @cache_entry_differs_when_packages_changed, @cache_entry_idempotent_when_status_unchanged,
      @cache_entry_differs_when_pull_secret_changed, @cache_entry_does_not_differ_when_no_status,
      @upsert_cache_entry_inserts_new, @upsert_cache_entry_updates_existing,
      @upsert_preserves_other_jukebox_entries, @upsert_no_op_when_no_status — the whole
      in-file `#[cfg(test)]` module, verified by `cargo test -p operator`.
  [ ] Cover the async cache accessors: @Context::upsert_jukebox_cache,
      @Context::remove_jukebox_cache and @Context::cache_needs_update over the locked map
      (present, absent key, double remove) — no test builds a @Context for this today;
      ./jukebox.rs touches them only through @reconcile.
  [ ] Cover @set_package_cache both arms — empty list keeps the old cache and warns, populated
      list wholesale-replaces and logs the counted info line; no test exists for the method.
  [ ] Cover @build_context: each env default and empty-value passthrough, the `base_context`
      key set, the seed on list @Ok/@Err, and the warn-only template-registration lane; no test
      exists.
  [ ] Cover @Manager::new failure lanes — client panic and each of the four probe panics — with
      a fake/unreachable cluster; no test exists; nothing spawns the binary either.
  [ ] Cover @Manager::metrics (order, EOF, encoder-failure continuation) and the
      @Manager::diagnostics snapshot against a @last_event write; no test exists.
  [?] @Context::set_package_cache is fully dead — zero call sites — while its empty-guard
      semantics differ from the live @build_context replace. Decide later whether it is deleted
      or wired to a live re-list lane.
  [?] A box whose @status is cleared keeps its cached packages forever (differs @false, upsert
      no-op): decide later whether status-removal must evict, refresh-with-empty, or add a TTL
      sweep — this cache has none.
  [?] A box that re-names or loses its name leaks old keys of the kinds in Handles; decide
      whether key churn gets a reaper or `""` keys are rejected outright.
  [?] @Diagnostics carries `#[serde(deserialize_with = "from_ts")]` although it derives no
      @Deserialize, and @from_ts is defined nowhere in the workspace — inert today, compile
      error the moment @Deserialize is added. Decide later: drop the attribute or define the
      deserializer with @Deserialize.
  [?] @Diagnostics.reporter is never serialized (@serde skip), never read, and its value
      (`vynil-controller` plus hostname) differs in kind from the event @Reporter that
      @common::context::get_reporter builds from @get_short_name and `POD_NAME`. Decide later
      whether it is replaced by that lane or deleted.
  [?] Template-dir failure is warn-only and a missing dir is a core silent no-op, so boot
      succeeds with a renderer whose partials are missing and the first failure surfaces
      mid-reconcile far from this file. Decide later whether @build_context must hard-fail on
      an absent `{CONTROLLER_BASE_DIR}/templates`.
  [?] The seed calls @JukeBox::@list — which builds a second @kube client through
      @get_client_async and can panic with a duplicate-text client-build panic — while
      @build_context already holds the process client and @JukeBox::@list_with_client exists.
      Decide later to pass the client down or keep the separate lane.
  [?] The controller-error drains in the @filter_map log nothing here, so a backoff storm is
      only visible if each kind's @error_policy says so — and those four are still pending
      specs. Decide later whether drained errors deserve a line at this layer.
  [?] The `/// Manager that owns a Controller for JukeBox, SystemInstance, and TenantInstance`
      doc omits @ServiceInstance although @new wires four; correct wording is a one-liner for
      the same slice that touches the file.
  [?] Startup-failure polarity here is @panic!-only (exit `101` per ./main.sdd) while its
      sibling boot failure (@bind) returns a @Result; the mixed-style decision lives in
      ./main.sdd's Tasks — resolve both lanes together there.

Done when:
  Every Scenario has a green mapped test or a decided `[?]` Task, the cache-lifetime and
    dead-lane decisions are recorded, and `cargo test -p operator`, `cargo clippy --all-targets
    -- -D warnings`, `cargo +nightly fmt --check` and `specdd lint` are green.

Scenario: An unstored JukeBox with status needs a cache entry
  Given an empty cache and a @JukeBox named `box-a` with a status
  When @cache_entry_differs runs
  Then the answer is @true — absent key outranks any payload — and @upsert_cache_entry inserts
    @status.packages under `box-a`
  Maps to tests @cache_entry_differs_when_not_in_cache, @upsert_cache_entry_inserts_new

Scenario: Changed packages or pull secret marks the entry stale, identical status does not
  Given a cached `box-a` entry
  When @cache_entry_differs sees packages differing in any element, or @spec.pull_secret
    differing from the cached @pull_secret, or a byte-identical status
  Then the first two answer @true and the third @false, and @upsert_cache_entry replaces the
    entry's payload while leaving sibling `box-b` entries untouched
  Maps to tests @cache_entry_differs_when_packages_changed,
    @cache_entry_differs_when_pull_secret_changed, @cache_entry_idempotent_when_status_unchanged,
    @upsert_cache_entry_updates_existing, @upsert_preserves_other_jukebox_entries

Scenario: A status-less JukeBox neither differs nor upserts
  Given a @JukeBox whose @status is @None
  When @cache_entry_differs and @upsert_cache_entry run on an empty or populated cache
  Then both answer @false / do nothing — the cache is never seeded, refreshed or evicted from a
    status-less box
  Maps to tests @cache_entry_does_not_differ_when_no_status, @upsert_no_op_when_no_status

Scenario: A missing CRD kills boot through the probes
  Given a reachable cluster missing, say, the @TenantInstance CRD and an installed @JukeBox CRD
  When @Manager::new runs
  Then the seed list succeeded or warn-logged, then the second probe @panic! with
    `is a CRD installed? {e}`
  And no future was returned, so ./main.rs never binds and the exit is `101`
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Environment defaults bake the base context once
  Given none of the six variables set
  When @build_context constructs @base_context
  Then the keys are exactly `vynil_namespace`:`vynil-system`,
    `agent_image`:`docker.io/sebt3/vynil-agent:0.7.7`, `service_account`:`vynil-agent`,
    `log_level`:`info`, `label_key`:`vynil.solidite.fr/tenant`
  But with `VYNIL_NAMESPACE` set to the empty string the value is `""`, and later env edits
    inside the live process change nothing here
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: A failed or empty seed still boots, with an empty cache
  Given @JukeBox::@list failing, or answering with only status-less boxes
  When @build_context finishes
  Then boot continues — @warn `While listing jukebox: {:?}` in the first case, debug pair lines
    in the second — and the cache ends empty regardless
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: set_package_cache refuses to empty a populated cache
  Given a cache holding entries and an @ObjectList of status-less JukeBoxes
  When @Context::set_package_cache runs
  Then the previous cache survives untouched and one @warn names the box list in parentheses
  But given a populated list, the cache is wholesale replaced after the counted @info line
  No mapped test exists — and no call site exists either (see Tasks `[?]`).

Scenario: Metrics text survives encoder failures
  Given a registry the text encoder rejects
  When @Manager::metrics encodes the four registries
  Then the failing registry is skipped with one @tracing::@error! line and the others — and the
    EOF leg — still encode, and the partial text is returned unchanged by the caller-side route
  No mapped test exists.

Example:
  future tuple destructure in ./main.rs: @Manager::@new().await resolves to the tuple
    destructured there as `manager` plus the @BoxFuture bindings `controller_jbs`,
    `controller_tnts`, `controller_stms` and `controller_svcs`
  env map → `base_context` keys: `CONTROLLER_BASE_DIR` stays private, `VYNIL_NAMESPACE` →
    `vynil_namespace`, `AGENT_IMAGE` → `agent_image`, `AGENT_ACCOUNT` → `service_account`,
    `AGENT_LOG_LEVEL` → `log_level`, `TENANT_LABEL` → `label_key`
  boot-time JSON on `GET /` before any reconcile: `{"last_event":"<boot instant>"}` — the only
    serialized @Diagnostics field
